```

The HCSA clusters map synthesizes these patterns into actionable categories. Red hotspots dominate, concentrated in established HDB estates across the north (Woodlands, Sembawang), central corridor (Bishan, Toa Payoh), west (Jurong, Clementi), and east (Tampines, Bedok, Pasir Ris). Notably absent are cold spots (blue), indicating no statistically significant clusters of low boarding activity. This pattern confirms morning peak demand originates predominantly from mature residential towns, with hotspots representing major commuter-generating neighborhoods requiring priority bus capacity and service frequency.

