### Perform Mann-Kendall test on Gi\* values

The Mann-Kendall test detects monotonic trends in bus ridership patterns over time:

-   H₀: No monotonic trend in ridership

-   H₁: Monotonic trend present

**Interpretation:**

Reject H₀ if p-value \< significance level (0.05)

Tau statistic (-1 to 1):

-   tau \> 0.3: Strong Upward

-   tau \> 0: Weak Upward

-   tau \< -0.3: Strong Downward

-   tau \< 0: Weak Downward

-   tau = 1: No Trend"

This identifies whether bus ridership is systematically increasing or decreasing across the analyzed time periods.

```{r}
#| code-summary: Function to perform Mann-Kendall test grouped by location

perform_mann_kendall <- function(gi_stars_df) {
  mk_results <- gi_stars_df %>%
    group_by(HEX_ID) %>%
    summarise(
      mk = list(
        unclass(
          Kendall::MannKendall(gi_star)
        )
      )
    ) %>%
    tidyr::unnest_wider(mk)
  
  return(mk_results)
}
```

::: panel-tabset

#### Weekday Morning Peak

```{r}
#| code-summary: Perform Mann-Kendall test
#| output: false
#| warning: false
#| error: false
#| message: false

mk_morning <- perform_mann_kendall(gi_stars_morning)
```

```{r}
#| code-summary: Select a few representative locations for preview

# Choose locations with different trend patterns

# Sort by significance and tau value to get diverse examples
mk_sorted <- mk_morning %>%
  arrange(sl) %>%
  mutate(trend_type = case_when(
    sl >= 0.05 ~ "Not Significant",
    tau > 0.3 ~ "Strong Upward",
    tau > 0 ~ "Weak Upward",
    tau < -0.3 ~ "Strong Downward",
    tau < 0 ~ "Weak Downward",
    TRUE ~ "No Trend"
  ))

# Select representative hexagons
selected_hexagons <- mk_sorted %>%
  group_by(trend_type) %>%
  slice_head(n = 5) %>%
  pull(HEX_ID)

print(mk_sorted %>% filter(HEX_ID %in% selected_hexagons))
```

In the above results, sl is the p-value. As all the hexagons show p-value \> 0.05, we will not reject the null hypothesis that there is no monotonic trend in ridership in any hexagon above.

Let's check if there is any hexagon having significant result.

```{r}
mk_morning %>% filter(sl < 0.05)
```

For weekday morning peak, as there is no hexagon having p-value \< 0.05, we will not reject the null hypothesis that there is no monotonic trend in ridership in any hexagon.

